    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Table&nbsp;2.01</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Differential diagnosis of conjunctival squamous intraepithelial neoplasia (CSIN)</span></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Hardeep Singh Mudhar",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 803.547px; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 115.531px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Diagnosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 162.75px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Histological features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 159.109px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Immunohistochemistry</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.297px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"16%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Other features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.984px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">References</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 115.531px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Conjunctival squamous intraepithelial neoplasia</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 162.75px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;1.2.2.1&gt;&gt;</span></span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Conjunctival squamous intraepithelial neoplasia</span></em> <span lang=\"EN-GB\">for histological details</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 159.109px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">p53+ in atypical cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CK17+ in atypical cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Loss of CK7 in atypical cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">p16 block positivity in cases associated with high-risk HPV</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.297px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"16%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Can be papillomatous</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.984px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;1.2.2.1&gt;&gt;</span></span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Conjunctival squamous intraepithelial neoplasia</span></em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{23786782}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 115.531px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Pigmented conjunctival squamous intraepithelial neoplasia</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 162.75px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Identical to CSIN except presence of hyperplastic dendritic melanocytes within dysplastic epithelium</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 159.109px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Similar to CSIN in the squamous population, but no expression in the melanocytic population</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.297px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"16%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Seen in patients with Fitzpatrick skin types&nbsp;IV&ndash;VI</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.984px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{11438062;6677848;1390513;974995}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 115.531px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Conjunctival intraepithelial neoplasia with mucinous differentiation</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 162.75px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Identical to CSIN except many atypical cells contain intracytoplasmic mucin at all levels of the dysplastic epithelium</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 159.109px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CK7+</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Patchy CK17 positivity</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">p16 block positivity in some cases</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.297px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"16%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Alcian blue&nbsp;/ PAS will stain the intracellular mucin</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Alternative terminology is &ldquo;adenosquamous carcinoma in&nbsp;situ&rdquo;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.984px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;1.2.2.3&gt;&gt;</span><em>Adenosquamous carcinoma</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{31932683;33619216}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 115.531px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Conjunctival sebaceous intraepithelial neoplasia</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 162.75px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Atypical intraepithelial cells with variable cytoplasmic lipidization arranged in a pagetoid and/or confluent pattern; preservation of the native basal epithelial layer is very common; in some cases, loss of the epithelial cells is seen, leaving a much-attenuated epithelium</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 159.109px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Intraepithelial sebaceous tumour cells stain for:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">adipophilin (vesicular cytoplasmic pattern)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">AR</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.297px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"16%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Purely intraepithelial lesions can exist</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.984px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;2.3.2.1&gt;&gt;</span><em>Sebaceous carcinoma</em></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 115.531px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Conjunctival melanocytic intraepithelial lesion</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 162.75px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Amelanotic melanocytic proliferation with varying degrees of cytological and architectural atypia; architectural patterns seen can be basal, pagetoid, nested, confluent</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 159.109px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Melanocytic proliferation stains for:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">melan-A</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">HMB45</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">SOX10</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.297px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"16%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Not relevant</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.984px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;1.3.2.1&gt;&gt;</span></span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Conjunctival melanocytic intraepithelial lesions</span></em><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{33002486}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 115.531px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Squamous metaplasia&nbsp;/ epidermalization</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 162.75px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Maintenance of epithelial polarity; acanthotic epithelium, which can manifest a granular cell layer, surface keratin and parakeratin, rete ridges, and loss of goblet cells; gradual transition with normal epithelium, rather than a sharp cut-off; basal cell hyperplasia which appears uniform horizontally across the lesion can be present; mitotic figures may be present but usually basal and no atypical forms</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 159.109px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Ki-67 usually confined to basal third of epithelium</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.297px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"16%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Check for a history of exposure (lid ectropion, chemosis), infection, injury, allergy, autoimmune disease, topical and systemic drug reactions, and vitamin&nbsp;A deficiency</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.984px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;1.1.2.1&gt;&gt;</span><em>Reactive epithelial hyperplasia of the conjunctiva</em></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 115.531px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Inflammation-associated epithelial atypia</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 162.75px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Maintenance of epithelial polarity; inflammatory cell percolation into epithelium that may be spongiotic and show basal vacuolar changes; basal cell hyperplasia which appears uniform horizontally across the lesion can be present; mitotic figures may be present but usually basal and no atypical forms</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 159.109px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Ki-67 is usually restricted to lower third of epithelium</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.297px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"16%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Check for a history of exposure (lid ectropion, chemosis), infection, injury, allergy, autoimmune disease, topical and systemic drug reactions</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.984px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;1.1.2.1&gt;&gt;</span><em>Reactive epithelial hyperplasia of the conjunctiva</em></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 115.531px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Topical chemotherapy&ndash;induced epithelial atypia</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 162.75px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Random atypia of squamous cells in superficial epithelial levels with smoky/smudgy nuclear chromatin in enlarged nuclei, but retention of N:C&nbsp;ratio; apoptotic cells, cytoplasmic eosinophilia, and stromal chronic inflammation sometimes seen</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 159.109px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Not relevant</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.297px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"16%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Usually in response to mitomycin&nbsp;C</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.984px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{10485547;10900099}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 115.531px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Hereditary benign intraepithelial dyskeratosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 162.75px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Sharply demarcated from normal conjunctiva; acanthosis, with substantial layered parakeratosis, with bright eosinophilic dyskeratotic squamous cells with pyknotic nuclei both within the epithelium and on the epithelial surface; no nuclear pleomorphism</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 159.109px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Not relevant</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.297px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"16%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Bilateral presentation; autosomal dominant condition (MIM number 127600)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.984px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;1.2.1.5&gt;&gt;</span><em>Hereditary benign intraepithelial dyskeratosis</em></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 115.531px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"17%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Benign squamous papilloma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 162.75px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Papillomatous lesion with fibrovascular cores, draped in non-dysplastic squamous epithelium, composed of elongated cells, associated with variable numbers of goblet cells and intraepithelial neutrophils; mitotic figures can be present but no atypical forms; surface keratinization is rare and when present occurs as a reactive change at the tips of the papilloma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 159.109px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Not relevant</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.297px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"16%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Mostly driven by HPV6 and HPV11</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 184.984px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"23%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">See <span class=\"ID-Section\" style=\"border: none;\">&lt;&lt;1.2.1.1&gt;&gt;</span></span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Conjunctival squamous papilloma</span></em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
